# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local object storage — REAL USER FILES.
#
# STORAGE_DRIVER=fs writes uploaded resumes and generated PDFs here, under
# .storage/resume/<userId>/<uuid>.pdf. Those are somebody's actual resume:
# name, address, phone number, employment history.
#
# It was not ignored, and a `git add -A` committed one. Anything the
# application writes at runtime belongs outside version control by default —
# the question is never "is this file sensitive" but "can the app create
# files here", and here it can.
.storage/
**/.storage/

# Scratch scripts. One-off probes written during debugging get swept up by
# `git add -A` and carry whatever query they were testing — which is how a
# personal email address ended up in a commit.
*-tmp.mjs
*-tmp.mts
*-tmp.js
*-tmp.ts
